  grid: 4 rows x 6 cols [observed]; generalizable to 4-8 rows x 6-12 cols (width must be even)
  colors: one background (0) + one foreground color; foreground is 2 [observed]
  rows: each row is either empty (all bg) or contains exactly 2 foreground markers mirrored across the vertical center
  markers: positions (k, W-1-k) for integer k in [0, W/2-1]; gap = W-1-2k (always odd)
  marker_rows: 2-4 per grid [observed]; empty_rows: 0-2 [observed]
  distinct_gap_levels: 1-3 per grid [observed]; at least 1 gap level required
  min_gap_rows: 1-2 rows share the minimum gap value
  transform: fill the horizontal span (inclusive) between the two markers on every row whose gap equals the minimum gap; all other rows unchanged
  edge_case: when min_gap == 1, markers are adjacent so fill adds nothing (output == input); occurs in 2/6 examples

